File Index

/.gitignore
Purpose: This file specifies patterns for files and directories that Git should ignore in a TypeScript project.

/CLAUDE.md
Purpose: This file defines repository-wide coding standards and AI interaction guidelines for consistent, secure, and high-quality code development.

/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
Purpose: Establishes community standards and enforcement for respectful participation.

/CONTRIBUTING.md
Purpose: This file outlines contribution guidelines, branching strategy, and standards for the Shattered Archive project.

/DISCLAIMER.md
Purpose: This file disclaims affiliation with referenced games and limits liability for software use.

/LICENSE
Purpose: This file establishes the licensing terms for the ShatteredArchive MUD Client, permitting non-commercial use, modification, and distribution while prohibiting monetization of the software or derivative works.

/LICENSE-COMMERCIAL
Purpose: This file outlines the terms for commercial use and licensing of ShatteredArchive software.

/LICENSING.md
Purpose: This file outlines the source-available licensing terms for ShatteredArchive software, permitting free use under specific conditions while requiring a commercial license for monetization.

/PRIVACY.md
Purpose: This file outlines how user data is collected, stored, and protected by the ShatteredArchive software.

/README.md
Purpose: This repository provides a monorepo codebase for a MUD tooling ecosystem including client, server, and shared packages.

/SECURITY.md
Purpose: This file outlines the security policy and vulnerability reporting procedures for the ShatteredArchive software project.

/SUPPORT.md
Purpose: Provides guidelines for reporting bugs, security issues, and seeking support for the community-driven ShatteredArchive project.

/ShatteredArchive.code-workspace
Purpose: This file configures a Visual Studio Code workspace including multiple related project directories.

/eslint.config.mjs
Purpose: Configures ESLint rules and settings for a TypeScript/JavaScript project with client and server distinctions.

/jest.config.cjs
Purpose: Aggregates Jest projects — delegates to package-local jest.config.cjs files (KT/mud-builder apps, engine, merc-area) and keeps generic server/client projects for the rest, with those packages excluded to avoid double runs.

/package.json
Purpose: This file manages project metadata, dependencies, and automation scripts for a multi-package Node.js application.

/pnpm-workspace.yaml
Purpose: Defines workspace packages and build configurations for a monorepo project.

/shatteredarchive-ai.code-workspace
Purpose: This file defines a multi-folder workspace configuration for the shattered archive AI project.

/shatteredarchive-mobile.code-workspace
Purpose: This file configures the Visual Studio Code workspace settings and folder structure for the shatteredarchive-mobile project.

/tsconfig.base.json
Purpose: Shared TypeScript compiler configuration settings for the project.

/tsconfig.jest.client.json
Purpose: Configures TypeScript compiler options for Jest client-side testing with custom path aliases.

/tsconfig.jest.json
Purpose: Configures TypeScript compiler options for Jest testing environment.

/tsconfig.jest.server.json
Purpose: Configures TypeScript compiler options for Jest server-side testing with Node.js module resolution.

/tsconfig.json
Purpose: This file configures TypeScript to reference multiple application projects within the workspace.
